<article class="env-definition" id="DA3E0C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/DA3E0C">Definition <span data-tag="DA3E0C">3.1.1.1</span>.</a>anodyne!markedmarked!anodyne The class of <em>marked anodyne</em> morphisms in $\mSet $ is the smallest weakly saturated (see §<a href="/tag/BC354B" data-tag="BC354B">8.1.2</a>) class of morphisms such that: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
For each $0 < i < n$, the inclusion $(\Lambda ^ n_ i)^{\flat } \subseteq (\Delta ^ n)^{\flat }$ is marked anodyne. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
For every $n >0$, the inclusion 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  ( \Lambda ^ n_ n, \calE \cap (\Lambda ^ n_ n)_{1} ) \subseteq ( \Delta ^ n, \calE ) \]
</div>
<p>
 is marked anodyne, where $\calE $ denotes the set of all degenerate edges of $\Delta ^ n$, together with the final edge $\Delta ^{ \{ n-1,n\}  }$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(3)$"><p>
The inclusion 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  (\Lambda ^2_1)^{\sharp } \coprod _{ (\Lambda ^2_1)^{\flat } } (\Delta ^2)^{\flat } \rightarrow (\Delta ^2)^{\sharp } \]
</div>
<p>
 is marked anodyne. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(4)$"><p>
For every Kan complex $K$, the map $K^{\flat } \rightarrow K^{\sharp }$ is marked anodyne. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
